  "notes": "Official cause code not provided in FORM-366 FIELDS (TBD/provisional per rule 4). Two LCO entry/exit periods (Aug 14-15 and Aug 24-27) were determined by Past Operability review to stem from the same underlying failed inlet fitting; modeled as a single continuous inoperability window (293 hours total, per narrative Section III.B) rather than two separate consequence nodes, consistent with the licensee's own aggregation. Note the narrative's Block 13 system code text is garbled ('D NUMBER NO. ~-I 002 1- 0'); LER number reconstructed as 446-2025-002-00 from docket 05000446 and event/report dates context. Unit 2 Train A Safety Chiller 2-05 was explicitly stated as 'remained operable throughout the duration of this event' but is the redundant train of the same CHS system rather than a distinct backup system, so it is represented via the sys_km System node with a role annotation rather than a separate System node. Similar-events section references only generic CAP trending, not a specific prior LER number, so no stub LER/SIMILAR_TO edge was created (per rule 9, only explicit referenced LER numbers are stubbed)."
